1. UU Remote protocol compatibility

The compatibility target is the UU Remote service provided by NetEase.
Protocol fields, message ordering, state transitions, and related behavior
are checked through reverse-engineering analysis of the official client and
its communication behavior. This implementation is not a NetEase SDK, an
official fork, or an officially certified client.

Rights in the names UU Remote and NetEase, official code, documentation,
marks, assets, and services belong to their respective rightsholders. The
project claims neither original authorship of the protocol nor ownership
or licensing of those rights. Running without official DLLs does not prove
that every part of the implementation is independently original, authorized,
or free of third-party rights.

Official terms entry point:
https://adl.netease.com/d/g/uuremote/c/licenseandservice?type=pc&direct=1
Project notices do not alter those service terms. Reverse engineering and
service access require separate assessment.

